# Sparky Stereo OS: the local FFmpeg build with Fraunhofer's AAC encoder (sparky-stereo-ffmpeg-fdk) is the one apt keeps.
# Its version is the edition's with +fdkN added; this puts it above the edition's own (priority 1001 for the repository),
# so an upgrade never swaps it for the build without the encoder. The rebuild for a newer FFmpeg comes from the helper.
# Nothing else carries +fdk in its version. Without this package the local build is just an installed version that
# apt puts back to the edition's at the next full-upgrade.
# (apt accepts a version pin only for named packages, not for "*": the names are the packages of the FFmpeg source,
# with globs for the numbered libraries and the -dev packages.)
Package: ffmpeg ffplay ffmpeg-doc libavcodec* libavdevice* libavfilter* libavformat* libavutil* libswresample* libswscale*
Pin: version *+fdk*
Pin-Priority: 1002
